    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Patrons and backing are in, and all 4 Playwright tests pass with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Storage:** a new `person_patron` table (`V23__person_patron.sql`). The database itself blocks naming the same patron twice and naming yourself.\n- **Server:** a new `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{id}/patrons` endpoint in `PersonService.addPatron`.\n  - It refuses a person naming themselves or a patron already named.\n  - When it succeeds it writes `PATRON_ADDED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 patron=\u2026`. A refused add writes nothing.\n  - Each person now also comes back with a `patronIds` list. The quick-add response includes it too.\n- **Screen:** each person's row has a patron dropdown, an \"Add patron\" button and a `person-patron-error` message.\n  - `person-patrons` shows the patrons' names, sorted and joined with \", \".\n  - `person-backing` adds up the patrons' due-totals, skips any that are n/a, and shows 0.00 when there are no patrons.\n  - Backing uses the same due-totals the screen already shows, so it updates straight away when something like a hold changes a patron's figure.\n  - The error clears when you pick another patron or take any other action on that row.\n\n**One behaviour to know about:** the dropdown doesn't list the person themselves, so you can't try to name yourself from the screen at all. The test accepts this, since it treats an option that isn't offered as a refusal. The server still refuses it with an error if the request arrives some other way. Naming someone who is already a patron is still offered, and the server refuses it with the error showing on the row.",
